## Code
- three.js r170 (MIT): loaded from the library's node_modules

## Images, models
- None. The Moon, the station, the telescope, the control room, the newspaper and the town are built in code. The
  photographs on paper are rendered at load from the film's own 3D Moon; no Luna 9 photograph, no external model or
  texture, no AI-generated image.

## Facts
- The dates, times, sizes and the story of the guessed ratio are sourced in demo/FACTS.md (NASA NSSDCA, Jodrell Bank,
  Science Museum Group, RussianSpaceWeb, Air & Space, NASA GSFC), with URLs and quoted wording.
- Invented for the film: the control room and its furniture, the log and card wording, the front page and its body
  copy, the kiosk and the town. The newspaper is not named and its masthead is not shown.
